<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is the difference between monorail and power-and-free?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A monorail conveyor connects all carriers to one continuously moving <a href="/conveyor-types/chain-conveyors/">chain</a>, every carrier moves at the same speed and cannot stop independently. A power-and-free conveyor uses two tracks: a power track with a moving chain and a free track with independent trolleys. Carriers engage and disengage from the chain, allowing individual stop, accumulation, and spur track routing.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What industries use these conveyors?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p><a href="/industries/automotive-conveyors/">Automotive manufacturing</a> is the largest user, power-and-free conveyors transport car bodies through paint shops and <a href="/industries/assembly-line-conveyors/">assembly lines</a>. Other major users include appliance manufacturing, aerospace component finishing, heavy equipment manufacturing, and general industrial coating operations (powder coating, wet paint, e-coat).</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">How fast do these conveyors run?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>The process sets the speed. Monorail runs at one constant speed. Power-and-free runs the power chain continuously while individual carriers stop, accumulate, or move at chain speed. Paint lines run slowly for dwell time in booths and ovens. Assembly lines match production takt time.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">How much weight can they carry?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>It depends on track size and trolley design. Ultimation rates its enclosed track trolley at 250 lbs and its 3-inch and 4-inch I-beam trolleys at 200 and 400 lbs, doubled with a load bar. It lists power-and-free unit loads up to 20,000 lbs. The building structure must support the total suspended load of track, chain, carriers, and products.</p>

</div>
</div>
